' Component Notes
note right of Deal
  <b>Real Domain Object</b>
  Concrete class with actual
  implementation that can be
  spied upon.

  Spies wrap real objects and
  delegate to real methods by
  default, allowing selective
  stubbing of specific methods.
end note

note left of Mockito
  <b>Spy Creation</b>
  spy(realObject) creates a wrapper
  that delegates to real methods
  unless explicitly stubbed.

  <b>Key Methods:</b>
  • spy() - Create spy wrapper
  • doReturn() - Stub without calling
  • when() - Stub (but calls method)
  • verify() - Verify interactions

  <b>Spy vs Mock:</b>
  spy() requires real object
  mock() creates empty shell
end note

note bottom of SpyWrapper
  <b>Spy Wrapper Mechanism</b>
  Wraps real object and intercepts calls:

  1. Check if method is stubbed
  2. If stubbed: return stubbed value
  3. If not: delegate to real method

  <b>State Sharing:</b>
  Spy and real object share state!
  Changes in spy affect real object.

  <b>Method Delegation:</b>
  • Stubbed methods → return stub
  • Real methods → execute actual code
end note

note right of Stubber
  <b>Safe Stubbing for Spies</b>
  Use doReturn().when() pattern:

  doReturn("value").when(spy).method();

  <b>Why not when().thenReturn()?</b>
  when(spy.method()).thenReturn("value")
  calls method FIRST, then stubs it.
  This can trigger unwanted side effects!

  <b>Best Practice:</b>
  Always use doReturn() for spies
  to avoid calling real method during
  stubbing.
end note

note bottom of MockObject
  <b>Mock (Empty Shell)</b>
  No real implementation.
  All methods return defaults:
  • Objects: null
  • Numbers: 0
  • Booleans: false
  • Collections: empty

  <b>Use When:</b>
  • Need complete control
  • Pure unit tests
  • Fast execution required
end note

note bottom of SpyObject
  <b>Spy (Real Object Wrapper)</b>
  Wraps real implementation.
  Methods call actual code:
  • Real logic executes
  • Real state changes
  • Real return values

  <b>Use When:</b>
  • Need partial mocking
  • Testing legacy code
  • Semi-integration tests
  • Most behavior should be real
end note

note right of MockitoSpyTest
  <b>Test Class Structure</b>
  Demonstrates spy capabilities:

  <b>Creation:</b>
  • spy(object)
  • @Spy annotation
  • Inline creation

  <b>Behavior:</b>
  • Real method calls
  • Selective stubbing
  • State sharing

  <b>Stubbing:</b>
  • doReturn().when()
  • doNothing() for void
  • doThrow() for exceptions

  <b>Verification:</b>
  • verify() real calls
  • verify() stubbed calls
  • InOrder verification
end note

